Debug profile 5 'no-subgroups': request a WebGPU device without the
Subgroups feature, so ggml-webgpu runs its workgroup-reduction shaders
instead of the subgroup ones. Same wasm binary, same harness page: the
profile selects the subgroup-free device per config, so a phone run can
compare subgroup-on vs subgroup-off directly.

The granted-device caps already re-derive supports_subgroups from the
device (patch 0007), and the correctness probe only compiles its subgroup
shader when subgroups are on, so no other change is needed: the probe
logs subgroups=false and the shader lib picks USE_WORKGROUP_REDUCTION.

Motivation: on the owner's POCO F5 Pro (Adreno 730) the Stage 0 bump did
not fix the garble — CPU correct, all three WebGPU configs the identical
deterministic garble from the first token — so subgroups are the top
remaining suspect (llama.cpp b12558 disabled Vulkan subgroup arithmetic
on Adreno for the same symptom class).

diff --git a/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-webgpu/ggml-webgpu.cpp b/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-webgpu/ggml-webgpu.cpp
--- a/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-webgpu/ggml-webgpu.cpp
+++ b/llama.cpp/ggml/src/ggml-webgpu/ggml-webgpu.cpp
@@ -4863,7 +4863,7 @@
     }
 }
 
-// 0 off, 1 amd-rdna3, 2 intel-arc, 3 no-f16, 4 reject-max-limits
+// 0 off, 1 amd-rdna3, 2 intel-arc, 3 no-f16, 4 reject-max-limits, 5 no-subgroups
 // Never invent a subgroup size (including a "wave64" debug override): a wrong
 // MAX_SUBGROUP_SIZE silently mistranslates.
 static int ggml_webgpu_debug_profile_code() {
@@ -4876,6 +4876,7 @@
                if (v === 'intel-arc') return 2;
                if (v === 'no-f16') return 3;
                if (v === 'reject-max-limits') return 4;
+               if (v === 'no-subgroups') return 5;
                return 0;
            });
 #else
@@ -5243,15 +5244,25 @@
     std::vector<wgpu::FeatureName> features_f16 = { wgpu::FeatureName::ShaderF16 };
     std::vector<wgpu::FeatureName> features_full = features_f16;
 
+    // Debug profile 5: request a device without the Subgroups feature, so the
+    // workgroup-reduction shaders run instead of the subgroup ones. The
+    // granted-device caps re-derive supports_subgroups below, and the
+    // correctness probe skips its subgroup shader when subgroups are off.
+    const bool no_subgroups = debug_profile == 5;
+    if (no_subgroups) {
+        GGML_LOG_INFO("ggml_webgpu: debug profile no-subgroups: requesting a device without Subgroups\n");
+        ggml_webgpu_disable_subgroups(ctx->webgpu_global_ctx->capabilities);
+    }
+
 #if !defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__) && !defined(__wasi__)
     features_f16.push_back(wgpu::FeatureName::ImplicitDeviceSynchronization);
     features_full.push_back(wgpu::FeatureName::ImplicitDeviceSynchronization);
-    if (ctx->webgpu_global_ctx->capabilities.supports_subgroup_matrix) {
+    if (!no_subgroups && ctx->webgpu_global_ctx->capabilities.supports_subgroup_matrix) {
         features_full.push_back(wgpu::FeatureName::ChromiumExperimentalSubgroupMatrix);
     }
 #endif
 
-    if (ctx->webgpu_global_ctx->capabilities.supports_subgroups) {
+    if (!no_subgroups && ctx->webgpu_global_ctx->capabilities.supports_subgroups) {
         features_full.push_back(wgpu::FeatureName::Subgroups);
     }
 
